WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.158
Debugger walkthrough, episode six.

2
00:00:02.158 --> 00:00:06.538
We answer one question, and follow that answer through the real code,

3
00:00:06.538 --> 00:00:08.760
line by line, with the real values.

4
00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:13.799
On control panel C P 1, the technician answers No to: power to lights.

5
00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:17.280
Watch the chip, the tab dot and the deficiency list.

6
00:00:17.632 --> 00:00:21.301
The field is now flagged, and the C P 1 tab shows a red dot.

7
00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:23.379
Let’s see how one click got there.

8
00:00:23.731 --> 00:00:25.693
We are paused in the Sources panel.

9
00:00:25.693 --> 00:00:27.599
The click lands in SegmentedField.

10
00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:30.907
This arrow function runs for the No button, and calls form.

11
00:00:30.907 --> 00:00:33.486
setValue() with the field name and the answer.

12
00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:36.277
Step in, and we are in setValue().

13
00:00:36.277 --> 00:00:38.788
Name is u4LightsPower, value is No.

14
00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:43.021
This one line is the only place the answer is stored: form.

15
00:00:43.021 --> 00:00:43.523
values.

16
00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:45.773
Then setValue() calls refresh().

17
00:00:45.773 --> 00:00:47.139
Refresh is a full pass.

18
00:00:47.139 --> 00:00:52.777
It updates every field and every widget, so nothing on screen keeps its own copy of the answer.

19
00:00:53.131 --> 00:00:56.242
During refresh, our field asks for its status.

20
00:00:56.242 --> 00:00:59.286
It has an evaluation rule: expectedValue Yes.

21
00:00:59.286 --> 00:01:02.600
So getStatus() hands the answer to the evaluator.

22
00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:04.542
Here is the evaluator.

23
00:01:04.542 --> 00:01:09.970
Value is No, the expected value is Yes, so it returns the fail status: red.

24
00:01:10.321 --> 00:01:12.718
And here the unit adds up its fields.

25
00:01:12.718 --> 00:01:17.318
hasFail is true, so CP-1 becomes red, with the label: deficiency found.

26
00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:19.327
That is the red dot on the tab.

27
00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.974
To try this yourself, open sample.

28
00:01:21.974 --> 00:01:26.768
html, open DevTools, and set the same breakpoints in the Sources panel.

29
00:01:26.768 --> 00:01:29.536
Then do what we did, and step through it.
